From eed3f807d21d3970220e99fab89615fd06289ae6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:02:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 102/105] test: add unit tests for the P2MR lattice tripwire
 parameters, options and state

p2mr_lattice_tripwire_tests checks:

- that the rules are not active on Ark-0, whose height and lattice
  tripwire outputs are not decided: ARK0_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE_HEIGHT is
  never, there are no outputs, and no block there executes leaf version
  0xe2 or fails ML-DSA-44 checks in it; that the default signet, the
  testnets and mainnet never activate them; and the static asserts on the
  order of the Ark-0 heights;
- the NUMS key of the first lattice tripwire output, computed again from
  "MLDSA44-NUMS/v1" and "lattice-tripwire/0" with the SHAKE256 of the
  vendored mldsa-native (bitcoin_mldsa_shake256, the only entry point the
  test uses), against its SHA256 constant, and the scriptPubKey of an
  output of the shape the three will have, against the value Python's
  hashlib gives;
- -signetlatticetripwire on a custom signet and on regtest, every
  dependency it needs and the order of the heights, its syntax,
  -testactivationheight=p2mr_lattice_tripwire@N, the default height of
  regtest, and the refusal on the chains it is not for;
- the state: present means unspent and created below the lattice height,
  not the height of the tripwire rules of leaf version 0xe0; any of three
  missing disables ML-DSA-44 checks; the two tripwires are independent;
- that ConnectBlock reads the state from the view it is given, as
  TestBlockValidity does: an ML-DSA-44 spend of leaf version 0xe2 with an
  invalid signature fails as an invalid signature in a view with the
  lattice tripwire output and as disabled without it, and a Schnorr spend
  of leaf version 0xe2 is valid in both (this code base has no ML-DSA-44
  signer; the functional test makes valid ones);
- the bits of the two flags, 27 and 28;
- with a checker that counts OP_CHECKMLDSA44 verifications: none once
  ML-DSA-44 is disabled in leaf version 0xe2, one otherwise and elsewhere;
- that the log of lattice tripwire spends skips the coinbase, on
  parameters with the null outpoint made directly, as the option refuses
  it;
- the option's edges: given twice, an outpoint twice, a height or a vout
  that does not fit, a null txid; regtest's default height following
  OP_CHECKMLDSA44 too, and the refusal of a final height below that of
  each of p2mr_mldsa44, p2mr_tripwire and p2mr_slhdsa128s;
- IsWitnessStandard for leaf versions 0xc0, 0xe0 and 0xe2: S1 and SLH1
  standard, S2 not in 0xe2, the 80-byte limit at depth one and zero, and
  template R1 of the rescue lane standard in 0xe0 and not in 0xe2.
